    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "seats is a read-write table keyed by the pair (hall bigint, seat integer) (D-row-key), so its pk is the JSON array of the two decimal texts, spelled the way Postgres prints jsonb: [\"1\", \"12\"].",
      "the insert names its key columns in columns, and they spell the pk, so it applies; the update names only a column outside the key; the delete targets the row by the same pk.",
      "the step-6 pull delivers the row under its composite pk and grants owner user-a, so the step-10 pull carries the tombstone the pushed delete left, under the same pk."
    ],
